---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title = "Postfire Debris Flows" sideBarActiveItemID="pfdfs">
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Postfire Debris Flows</div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-2 mb-6">
      <text class="text-lg prose">
      I lead the effort to build, scale, and deploy the
      <a href="https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/6818f950d4be0208bc3e0165">PWFDF Collection</a>,
      the USGS's official postfire debris-flow (PFDF) hazard assessment product. Over my tenure,
      I've modernized this product from a collection of unpublished legacy scripts
      to a production-grade, open-source software stack. These improvements have allowed
      us to scale these assessments to a publicly-released, national hazard product, complete
      with a strict data specification and access API.
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-2">Related Work</div>
  </div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="PWFDF Collection"
    img="/postfire/pwfdf-map-2.png"
    desc="The USGS's official postfire debris-flow hazard assessment product."
    url="/postfire-debris-flows/pwfdf"
    badge="Data Archive & Standards"
  /> 

  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Data API"
    img="/postfire/pwfdf-api.png"
    desc="Search, query, and download hazard assessment data from the PWFDF Collection."
    url="/postfire-debris-flows/pwfdf-api"
    badge="API"
  /> 

  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Production Pipeline"
    img="/postfire/ocelote.png"
    desc="The USGS's in-house pipeline for producing and publishing PFDF hazard assessments."
    url="/postfire-debris-flows/ocelote"
    badge="Infrastructure"
  /> 

  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Hazard Modeling Toolkit"
    img="/postfire/pfdf-cropped.png"
    desc="Core libraries for analyzing, modeling, and mapping PFDF hazard assessments."
    url="/postfire-debris-flows/toolkit"
    badge="Python, CLI"
  /> 

  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-4 mt-8">More Info</div>
  </div>

  For more details, here's a seminar I gave about this work at the Geologic Hazards Science Center:

  <div class="border-base-300 pt-10 non-prose">
    <div class="aspect-video w-full max-w-3xl rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-md bg-neutral">
      <iframe
        class="w-full h-full"
        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/aYXB4cc0lCI?si=Mq_lotB8jx2kWwsc"
        title="GHSC Seminar 2026-02-17"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
        allowfullscreen>
      </iframe>
    </div>
  </div>

